---
/**
 * Four rings, drawn one inside the other: artificial intelligence, machine
 * learning, deep learning, generative AI.
 *
 * The nesting is the argument, so it is carried by geometry rather than by
 * colour — each ring is physically inside the last, and every band states in
 * words what it is, one thing it is, and how it fails. Read the right-hand
 * column top to bottom and you get the unit's whole claim: the further in you
 * go, the less anyone can say about why an answer came out.
 *
 * Colour does no work here (hard rule 9). The alternating fills only separate
 * the bands; every distinction is also spelled out in text, and the innermost
 * ring is marked by position and label as much as by tint.
 *
 * Decorative on its own, so `aria-hidden`: `Figure` supplies the accessible
 * name and the description.
 */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 640 520" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
  <!-- Ring 1 — artificial intelligence. The widest and oldest circle. -->
  <rect
    x="8"
    y="8"
    width="624"
    height="504"
    rx="14"
    class="fill-paper stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.25"></rect>

  <text
    x="26"
    y="36"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="14"
    font-weight="700">Artificial intelligence</text
  >
  <text x="26" y="56" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="10"
    >any machine doing a job that seems to need a person</text
  >
  <text x="26" y="74" class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="10"
    >e.g. a chess program from 1985, following rules a person wrote</text
  >
  <text
    x="614"
    y="36"
    text-anchor="end"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="10">fails: stops at the edge of what was written down</text
  >

  <!-- Ring 2 — machine learning. -->
  <rect
    x="44"
    y="86"
    width="552"
    height="402"
    rx="12"
    class="fill-paper-sunken stroke-rule-strong"
    stroke-width="1.5"></rect>

  <text
    x="62"
    y="114"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="14"
    font-weight="700">Machine learning</text
  >
  <text x="62" y="134" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="10"
    >never told the rule &mdash; it settles on one from examples</text
  >
  <text x="62" y="152" class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="10"
    >e.g. the fraud check that decides your card looks stolen</text
  >
  <text
    x="578"
    y="114"
    text-anchor="end"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="10">fails: goes wrong quietly on unfamiliar cases</text
  >

  <!-- Ring 3 — deep learning. -->
  <rect
    x="80"
    y="164"
    width="480"
    height="300"
    rx="10"
    class="fill-paper stroke-ink-muted"
    stroke-width="1.75"></rect>

  <text
    x="98"
    y="192"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="14"
    font-weight="700">Deep learning</text
  >
  <text x="98" y="212" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="10"
    >the same dials, stacked in many layers, one feeding the next</text
  >
  <text x="98" y="230" class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="10"
    >e.g. the app that finds every photo of your dog</text
  >
  <text
    x="542"
    y="192"
    text-anchor="end"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="10">fails: no traceable reason for any answer</text
  >

  <!-- Ring 4 — generative AI. The innermost, and where chatbots live. -->
  <rect
    x="116"
    y="242"
    width="408"
    height="198"
    rx="8"
    class="fill-accent-soft stroke-accent"
    stroke-width="2"></rect>

  <text
    x="134"
    y="270"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="14"
    font-weight="700">Generative AI</text
  >
  <text x="134" y="290" class="fill-ink-muted font-mono" font-size="10"
    >produces new material instead of choosing between options</text
  >
  <text x="134" y="308" class="fill-ink-faint font-mono" font-size="10"
    >e.g. the chatbot that wrote your birthday message</text
  >
  <text
    x="506"
    y="270"
    text-anchor="end"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="10">fails: invents plausible untruths</text
  >

  <!-- The consequence, stated where the innermost ring has room for it. -->
  <text
    x="320"
    y="370"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink font-display"
    font-size="13"
    font-weight="700">a chatbot sits in all four rings at once</text
  >
  <text
    x="320"
    y="392"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-muted font-mono"
    font-size="9.5"
    >so every failure listed above is also one of its failures</text
  >

  <!-- The rule the whole picture depends on. -->
  <text
    x="320"
    y="502"
    text-anchor="middle"
    class="fill-ink-faint font-mono"
    font-size="9"
    >nothing sits in an inner ring without also sitting in every ring outside it</text
  >
</svg>
